# API Information


main: {
  kit: {
    info: {
      contact: {
        email: "dev@tryterra.co"
        name: "Terra API"
        url: "https://tryterra.co/"
      }
      description: `The Terra API (v2 surface, served at access.tryterra.co/api/v2). Protected product operations require a current product entitlement in addition to valid credentials and token scopes. Missing access returns HTTP 403 with code entitlement_required; disabled environments return environment_disabled. Unavailable current authorization returns HTTP 503 with code authorization_unavailable. Billing, configuration and recovery remain available under their existing permissions. Completed Health Scores stay with the caller's own authorized data. Pass recipients require their own Health Scores entitlement; otherwise enrichment fields retain null values. New score computation requires Health Scores access. Retained lab reports remain readable through the report endpoints with valid credentials and ownership, without a current Lab Reports entitlement. New uploads and reprocessing require it.

**Lab reports versioning.** The report endpoints (\`/reports\`, and the deprecated \`/lab-reports\`) are versioned by date. Send \`X-Terra-Version: <date>\` to choose the version a request is served in: the newest version on or before that date. Without the header a request gets the environment's pinned version. An environment without a pin is pinned to the latest version on its first request; change the pin through the admin API (\`PUT /api/v3/admin/environments/{dev_id}/lab-reports/api-version\`). Every authenticated response carries \`X-Terra-Version\` stating the version it was served in, and every \`lab_report\` webhook delivery carries the environment's version. A malformed or future date returns 400 with code \`invalid_api_version\`. Versions are \`2026-10-21\` (latest: the report list is paginated) and \`2026-03-24\` (the list returns up to 500 reports in \`sessions\`). This document describes the latest version.
`
